  "question": {
    "text": "The magnetic moments associated with two closely wound circular coils <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively are equal if: (Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> are number of turn and current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> respectively)",
    "image": null
